{"id": "clm:8d68256445c8f4435cb333a7bf68d28c72b6a822b576649345a08c43a48cf90e", "type": "statement", "text": "GridFS splits files into chunks, using a default chunk size of 255 KiB, with a final chunk only as large as necessary. It uses separate collections for file chunks and metadata and can store files larger than the 16 MiB BSON document limit. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/gridfs.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06f72376ea73a3eb05348609fc7aa207bce65fbfa425f3a7f6e324d664ea5a08"]}
{"id": "clm:0443f5c4d3c5214a672f717c2223668aac754dcb33e44e83656972d497b04577", "type": "statement", "text": "`get_regex` downloads files matching a regular expression and cannot use `--local`; a multi-filename `get` also cannot use `--local`. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6987ade77bce0c8ab6dc62005d0895d2d478afa3176db0944396b4bbbce7d365", "ev:ded43c847142026effafd434cca657bf49687eddbd2f1b49f5b3f419f13d9146"]}
{"id": "clm:2ceda8c073ec4072a9c530e385c2e50608393a4ac7a5d7bd0e7b2ff16483342d", "type": "statement", "text": "`bsondump` is a system-command-line tool for viewing and debugging BSON files as human-readable JSON. MongoDB describes it as a diagnostic tool rather than a data ingestion tool. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/bsondump.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ecaafaea92c308c141625ae3e034d03a1302c45e6565f494bfc1c8ccae83d56", "ev:b23296d20066ffb115eec30488601ea0fe16f960149bc918a23fec67e7e26716"]}
{"id": "clm:b08cfb446e0b8f2f3c0ac54e25b1a750865c2edb15c147a5dafc5978d77b5782", "type": "statement", "text": "`--local` selects a local filename for upload or download when it differs from the GridFS name; multi-file get cannot use this option. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9698d5b3ea6221a0741eda0267a94f3cdcd4d504c677169ff1b151ac4dbb2dc0", "ev:ded43c847142026effafd434cca657bf49687eddbd2f1b49f5b3f419f13d9146"]}
{"id": "clm:4eb750c5007589bc23f7ef1513ce4af62aad54edd5a3c9e4d3ffd5f066a0b655", "type": "statement", "text": "Without `--replace`, `mongofiles put` adds another GridFS object with the same name instead of overwriting an existing one. `--replace` changes this behavior; the Kali-distributed help describes removing other same-name files after put. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5375f0aea09ec4a00ef427247ff29c02ba02dbb6fff0049d554eac38478948e8", "ev:eaf8b5437c0822ee60e7a28068d02040c1abecf383176b6e2c5f14fe74319ec6"]}
{"id": "clm:ed75b8f1447c7f2ba42814f5853faba2dd05d1f0b252d5c9ef9904b6d3f72577", "type": "statement", "text": "`bsondump` formats output as Extended JSON v2.0 in Canonical mode. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/bsondump.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6e10749a33e0e36e1592b8f59ace029a9481af379c40a39158937470801f4566"]}
{"id": "clm:6bcfe933a452bdfca6456dcd32acfc0dce256f96c056b8ec6e1ca01600c89686", "type": "statement", "text": "For a local BSON file, `bsondump --outFile=collection.json collection.bson` writes readable JSON to collection.json. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/mongodb-how-to-convert-bson-documents-to-a-human-readable-format/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/bsondump.md", "https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7f6e25b49a6d72910a20657285cfd759de70836a45d4d730889bf9c3d8b00ad3", "ev:b59e6ec789a71c876d7c8f58ff2347a0f02849c33c489574545e3822b45d08a5"]}
{"id": "clm:b8eed15d4b149381468c4b68c73dff6d51408c4d20ec3a44bca31103084fd659", "type": "statement", "text": "`bsondump` reads standard input and writes standard output by default; `--bsonFile` and `--outFile` select explicit input and output paths. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/bsondump.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:401716ad095f2f62d66d7f7434745d4c145baa5f1ed52fd48c1bc7baa3b7bd08", "ev:f04af843580be1b2a076685ed9bd8d8d92b2e2bcf2bb46c2c154af179065d171"]}
{"id": "clm:242440cfe359dc66742260c8e526b66c5f32eaf64c493dbd333b7004c3fd385c", "type": "statement", "text": "mongofiles provides command-line operations between local files and GridFS, including upload, download, listing, searching, and deletion. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3eb50a01aa91f0ce43126df93efbb9c6dd11e19a49972cd11f921725f2d854fc", "ev:a0e67ab3888dfa06f4778914586d656ad99912c0af737be5e6f178acc3f4a1e8"]}
{"id": "clm:2c68d4b04d63781f1dc664fbd17d146dc8a66df4a081d9089f749e3060a1c6ba", "type": "statement", "text": "GridFS divides files into chunks and metadata collections; its default bucket uses `fs.chunks` and `fs.files`, with default chunks of 255 KiB. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/gridfs.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a1a4fc4a58279bbf4d92011481f2065dc737aa7cf49100486dc465448f43f22c", "ev:d75dca0e7f352b600f99d2e608309186bab831801538037f07441aa8e21bfb13"]}
{"id": "clm:8140c0ca3482b0aa523ca65398d442d9a859226cca1d33fc73885153219bf305", "type": "statement", "text": "`mongofiles -d=records put 32-corinth.lp` uploads the local file, while `mongofiles -d=records get 32-corinth.lp` downloads it. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ab7bdcf605d246a21c637e763d7282a537060c71f28d395c14ac485536f3af0e", "ev:c876d04b0753e2711ac2c0585cdbe5af9f414ed014dc85e9c5208786e0f29b8d"]}
{"id": "clm:ac85068cc400f592714d1a29879a03eccba176c5aca1a2b7ab4b137abe5def5c", "type": "statement", "text": "`list` accepts an optional filename prefix; `search` finds filenames matching a pattern within the name. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:26bf8e9430402925ee536cee015634c1ce171885439f8de24461354236f494e3", "ev:67d1a7a28151cbdfea19680386146c8674b57d6515e2de9e671e66ab32708e44"]}
{"id": "clm:6af782c3323658a8eecd0e39c7fdcd9d06fe3cb7681c496cdce95339f5b79bdb", "type": "statement", "text": "GridFS does not support multi-document transactions or atomic updates of an entire file. MongoDB recommends uploading a new version, atomically switching a metadata field that marks the latest version, then removing old versions as needed. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/gridfs.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:988f6fcf6de3d21af974f700a7c207983923be2b8e0652a87c8af1f017afa668", "ev:eaa52c740ec58dd112b430439c6f99caa7a867680ea97ff40b6222baa5b5a28b"]}
{"id": "clm:369e7bdbbf82da3c6c2d61f23b9dd86a69b14ca5c0ec8c2a6139733ac51f2da3", "type": "statement", "text": "`mongofiles` moves files between the local filesystem and GridFS from the system command line. Its syntax is `mongofiles <options> <connection-string> <command> <filename or _id>`. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:26bf8e9430402925ee536cee015634c1ce171885439f8de24461354236f494e3", "ev:5a451ebdf8f5622b748e47acd305b92690454d07008fcec488166769f6908639"]}
{"id": "clm:d73aeacc92d05ac5eb5f19f5f49cde4182b05157c49b7585e026bf9421934514", "type": "statement", "text": "`mongofiles -d=records list` lists files in the records database. `list` optionally filters by filename prefix; `search` finds matching filenames, with the Kali-distributed help identifying its argument as a regex. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:26bf8e9430402925ee536cee015634c1ce171885439f8de24461354236f494e3", "ev:642d0888d0986739ef4c326982f96dac7661e6b91ea75e223e4312009e6da17c", "ev:67d1a7a28151cbdfea19680386146c8674b57d6515e2de9e671e66ab32708e44"]}
{"id": "clm:05532435b0fe98ec2c51a6dd380542e8e35a9f8b17628ced1eab5eab6e8180d4", "type": "statement", "text": "`mongofiles -d=records put 32-corinth.lp` uploads a local file; `mongofiles -d=records get 32-corinth.lp` downloads the named GridFS file. `--local` supplies a different local filename for put or get. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.kali.org/tools/mongo-tools/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:391cf3180b9067f4b325f926b28e74b9701f0f5352b790608f9e0d6f0d24000d", "ev:9698d5b3ea6221a0741eda0267a94f3cdcd4d504c677169ff1b151ac4dbb2dc0", "ev:98d0cfd76030b9d24bee6a05354e34fed492b17db0cb6ef8f3c2bc7e588cff5f"]}
{"id": "clm:0aa7a8ed5fad2c2b664416ecfb6676273c46539224c92824174af898e0703a5e", "type": "statement", "text": "For authorized access, MongoDB documents the `read` role for `list`, `search`, and `get`, and `readWrite` for `put` and `delete` on the accessed database. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongofiles.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["bsondump and mongofiles (GridFS) usage"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06f99f67422aa81a2b6a709b4ae020ea3bdbc131690ca967e6e940b803c3f605", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6a8dc4d97c4098df87a7a2c4a63cf05869db4e0fb76d499bb281a76966fd42aa"]}
